From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.globalization: DecimalFormatter and number rounders

WinUI 2's NumberBox (Windows Terminal's settings: launch size, positions, and many more) makes a DecimalFormatter for the user's language and a SignificantDigitsNumberRounder in its constructor; neither existed, so no NumberBox could be made. Windows.Globalization.NumberFormatting now has DecimalFormatter (formatting with integer, fraction and significant digit minimums, grouping and the language's decimal and grouping separators, through its NumberRounder; parsing the same text back, null for text that is no number), SignificantDigitsNumberRounder and IncrementNumberRounder (all eleven rounding algorithms). Latin digits only: another numeral system is kept, not used. CurrencyFormatter, PercentFormatter, PermilleFormatter and NumeralSystemTranslator are not made yet.
---
